# All-theme workflow

- Daily work stays on `main` and pushes to `wallet/main` unless James explicitly asks otherwise.
- Discover every registered client from `build/themes.json`; currently they are `clients/safe` and `clients/etx`.
- Apply every applicable user-facing feature, fix, and behavior change independently to every registered client unless James explicitly limits the request to one theme.
- Before finishing, compare all client implementations and tests. Do not assume matching files stayed equivalent.
- Keep the client trees isolated. Never import one client from another or replace one UI with the other.
- `THEME=safe` or `THEME=etx` selects exactly one client at Vite startup/build time.
- Preserve storage identities: Safe uses `elmsafe`; ETX uses `etwallet`.
- Shared behavior must be extracted through a neutral package with contract tests, not by cross-client imports.
- Run focused tests for every changed client and `npm run test:themes` for all-theme or shared-infrastructure changes.
- After every user prompt that changes the running app, rebuild the Safe production bundle (`THEME=safe`) and restart the process on port 8080.

# Commit and push confirmation

- A commit/push request includes all applicable registered-client changes and their tests.
- After a successful requested commit or push, end the user-facing confirmation with `🗂️` only after verifying all registered clients were covered.
- If any client was intentionally excluded, do not use `🗂️`; name the excluded client and reason instead.
